\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Search Themes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Google\'92s Explanation:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf0 Performance Max currently looks at your assets, feeds, and landing pages to predict which placements, including search queries, will perform well for your campaign. Now with the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/13351809?sjid=7788560555771332292-NA"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 search themes}}\'a0beta, you can fill in gaps by adding information about your business that you expect to perform well. By combining your expertise with Google AI you\'92ll be able to expand your reach on all channels, including Search.
\f1\i0 \

\f2\i Here are a few examples where search themes can be especially helpful if you have knowledge about your business or customers that AI can\'92t easily or quickly learn:
\f1\i0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Your landing page doesn\'92t have complete details or the latest updates about the products and services you offer.
\f1\i0 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You\'92ve just expanded into a new market or launched a new product or service where your campaigns don\'92t have extensive performance history.
\f1\i0 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You are launching a new promotion or sale for the holiday season where you don\'92t have extensive performance history.
\f1\i0 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You want to expand your reach within Performance Max\'97including on Search inventory in Performance Max\'97and ensure you have comprehensive coverage on important business themes.
\f1\i0 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You want to provide important information to help your campaign ramp up and optimize performance faster.
\f1\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\i\b \cf0 When you add search themes, you\'92re telling Google AI you want to reach that traffic in your Performance Max campaign across all Google Ads inventory including Search, YouTube, Gmail, Discover, Maps, and Display. Search themes also help you find audiences across channels based on users\'92 search behavior.
\f1\i0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Simple Explanation:
\f1\b0  Search Themes are just a new additional signal that help bridge the gap between what Google will know what to target based on your landing pages, assets, or product feed\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 How Search Themes work?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Google\'92s Explanation:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf0 Here\'92s how it works:
\f1\i0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\i \cf3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/13351809"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Search themes}}\cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'a0let you indicate queries that you know your customers are looking for. They are optional and are additive to what queries Performance Max would match you to using your URLs, assets, and more.
\f1\i0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You can add up to 25 search themes per asset group.
\f1\i0 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Search themes will respect\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/13721847?#Pmax"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 brand exclusions in Performance Max}}\'a0and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/11396330"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 account-level negative keywords}}.
\f1\i0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\i\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Results driven from search themes will bring your customers to the landing pages you\'92ve indicated via your\'a0[Final URL expansion]({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/sa360/answer/12367110?#:~:text=Final"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 https://support.google.com/sa360/answer/12367110?#:~:text=Final}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/sa360/answer/12367110?#:~:text=Final%20URL%20expansion%20helps%20you,matches%20your%20landing%20page%20content.)"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3  URL expansion helps you,matches your landing page content.)}},\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/7166527"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 page feeds}}, and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/11189316#urlcontains"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 URL contains}}\'a0settings.
\f1\i0\b0 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\i\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Search themes will have the same prioritization as your phrase match and broad match keywords in your Search campaigns.
\f1\i0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You\'92ll be able to see the search categories that your ads matched to in your\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/11386930"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 search terms insights}}\'a0at both the campaign and account levels, and associated conversion performance. You can now view search term insights for custom date ranges, download your data, and access it via the API.
\f1\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14179631#:~:text=In"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14179631#:~:text=In}} early 2024%2C we'll,interests will still be available.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Simple Explanation:
\f1\b0  Search Themes work like Audience Signals and are just signals to Google. They are not targeting!\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Search priority\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Google\'92s Explanation:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf0 On Search inventory specifically,\'a0Search themes will have the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/2756257"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 same prioritization as your phrase match and broad match keywords}}\'a0in your Search campaigns and the one with the highest Ad Rank will be prioritized.
\f1\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
